Code a B_PRED macroblock once, not twice, on a key frame.

Applied after libvpx-vp8-copy-only-what-changed.patch.

In realtime mode vp8_pick_intra_mode() tries B_PRED last, and its 4x4 search
has to code every subblock with the mode it picks before picking the next:
the next subblock predicts from those reconstructed pixels. It does that with
vp8_encode_intra4x4block(), and when B_PRED wins, vp8cx_encode_intra_macroblock()
then calls vp8_encode_intra4x4mby() -- the same sixteen calls on the same
inputs in the same order -- and throws the first result away. Nothing touches
the luma state in between, and B_PRED can only win once all sixteen are coded
(the search gives up early only by returning INT_MAX). So the second pass is
skipped. Not with the RD picker, which tries modes in another order, nor with
SSIM tuning, which moves the quantizer between picking and coding.

A key frame is what every session starts with and what every refresh and
scale change costs: 2.3 s at 1280x1024 on an O2. Sampled under IRIS (the key
frame is arithmetic, so the emulator's proportions hold), the transform and
the quantizer were a third of it, and on text, where B_PRED wins nearly
everywhere, sixteen of every forty transforms were this repeat.

THE BITSTREAM IS UNCHANGED: `encfloor verify` hashes identically with and
without it; see the commit that added this file for the numbers.

--- a/vp8/encoder/encodeframe.c
+++ b/vp8/encoder/encodeframe.c
@@ -1203,7 +1203,30 @@
   }
 
   if (x->e_mbd.mode_info_context->mbmi.mode == B_PRED) {
-    vp8_encode_intra4x4mby(x);
+    /* Already done, when the realtime picker chose it.
+     *
+     * vp8_pick_intra_mode() tries B_PRED last, and pick_intra4x4mby_modes()
+     * has to code each subblock with the mode it picks before it can pick the
+     * next one -- the next subblock predicts from those reconstructed pixels.
+     * It does that through vp8_encode_intra4x4block(), the very function
+     * vp8_encode_intra4x4mby() would call, on the same inputs in the same
+     * order, and nothing touches the luma state in between: so when B_PRED
+     * wins, the quantized coefficients, the eobs and the reconstruction are
+     * already exactly what coding the macroblock again would produce. (It
+     * can only win after coding all sixteen: the search gives up early only
+     * by returning INT_MAX, which never beats the 16x16 result.)
+     *
+     * Coding it again was sixteen more predict, subtract, transform, quantize
+     * and reconstruct passes per macroblock -- on text, where B_PRED wins
+     * nearly everywhere, a large share of a key frame, which is what every
+     * session starts with and every refresh costs. Not with the RD picker,
+     * which tries modes in another order, nor with SSIM tuning, which moves
+     * the quantizer between picking and coding. */
+    const int picked_realtime =
+        !(cpi->sf.RD && cpi->compressor_speed != 2);
+    if (!picked_realtime || cpi->oxcf.tuning == VP8_TUNE_SSIM) {
+      vp8_encode_intra4x4mby(x);
+    }
   } else {
     vp8_encode_intra16x16mby(x);
   }
